 "honest_note": "PAM/PPL1 OPPONENT ORGANIZATION: the mushroom body is tiled into compartments, each co-innervated by dopaminergic neurons (DANs) and mushroom body output neurons (MBONs). PAM-cluster DANs (reward.json: 'dopaminergic PAM neuron 1') innervate APPETITIVE compartments and drive approach learning; PPL1-cluster DANs (this file: PPL1-gamma1pedc + PPL1-alpha3) innervate AVERSIVE compartments and drive avoidance learning. Same MB architecture, opponent valence \u2014 reward and punishment are the two halves of one teaching signal. Query notes: general 'dopaminergic PPL1 neuron' (FBbt_00100219) fails server-side in all forms; 'dopaminergic PPL1 neuron 2' fails; MB-SV (FBbt_00110323) returns 0 rows \u2014 all logged in GAPS.md. hop0 is a documented merge of the two canonical aversive PPL1 DANs whose connectivity is indexed."
